{title: Even the Wind and the Sea}
{subtitle: Mark 4:35–41; Matthew 8:23–27; Luke 8:22–25}
{key: D#m}
{tempo: 130}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [D#m] | ×24

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
Why are you so afraid?
Do you still have no faith?
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
He got up and rebuked the wind
Quiet! Be still!
The wind died down, and there was a great calm
Who is this?
Even the wind and the sea obey him!
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Let's cross over to the other side, he said when evening fell
We left the crowd along the shore and rode into the swell
[B]The sky went black, the squall came down, the water [A#]filled the hull
And Jesus in [D#m]the stern was [D#m]sleeping on a cushion [F#]through [G#sus2]it [D#m]all
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Pre-Chorus}
Teacher, don't you care that we're going to [F#]drown?
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
He [G#sus2]got [B]up and rebuked the wind
[C#]Quiet! Be still! [D#m]
The wind died down, and there was a great calm
Who is this?
Even the wind and the sea obey him!
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
We bailed with buckets, bailed with hands, we shouted through the roar
The waves broke over every side, we could not see the shore
We fishermen who knew the lake were certain we would drown
And still he slept there in the stern while the [B]sea was crashing down
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Pre-Chorus}
Teacher, don't you care that [A#]we're going to drown?
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
He got [D#m]up and re[D#m]buked the wind
Quiet! [F#]Be [G#sus2]still!
[D#m]The wind died down, and there was a great calm
[F#]Who is [G#sus2]this?
[B]Even the wind and the [C#]sea obey him!
{end_of_chorus}

